  "answer_text": "Here is how you can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 Direct Login Link\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Click here to sign in to My Service Canada Account (MSCA)](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n## Sign-In Options\n\nYou can log in using **one of the following methods**:\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfe6 Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner\nThis allows you to register or sign in using your **online banking information** to access MSCA.\n\n### 2. \ud83d\udd11 GCKey\nGCKey allows you to access **multiple Government of Canada online services**. If you already have a GCKey username and password, you can use it to log in.\n\n### 3. \ud83e\udeaa Provincial Sign-In (Alberta & BC only)\nYou can access MSCA by signing in or registering with your **provincial sign-in**, but this service is only available for residents of **Alberta and British Columbia**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udd95 New User? How to Register\n\nIf you don't have an account yet:\n- Click **\"Start your registration\"** to create a GCKey username and password. To create an account, you need to apply for a **Social Insurance Number (SIN)**.\n- **PACs (Personal Access Codes)** are used to verify your identity when registering for MSCA. If you already applied for CPP/OAS benefits, your PAC has been sent to you **by mail**.\n\n---\n\n> \u26a0\ufe0f **Security Reminder:** You must access and use MSCA **only as yourself**. No one is authorized to use or create an account on your behalf.\n\nIf you need further help, you can contact **Service Canada at 1-800-206-7218**.",
